WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.660
Barkley is buying over a million Tesla shares after three quarters of selling shows institutions returning despite mixed market signals. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 575. After three straight quarters of net selling, Barkley's added $1,16,703 shares. Those shares were worth $427,625,000. The bank now holds $11,521,936 shares.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:55.820
Valueed at $4,846,000. That position represents 1.5313% of its $316.48 billion portfolio. The move reverses a prior selling streak and signals renewed institutional accumulation. Daily price action remains driven by net supply and demand, with some institutions buying, while others plus retail and Shorts sell more.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:04.600
While institutions signal renewed interest in the stock, regulatory developments in Europe show Tesla still needs to prove the technology on the ground.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:16.940
Tesla FSD received activation permission in the Netherlands, the first European country to allow it. Early driver reports highlight questions around local signage, markings, and road behavior.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:34.040
The rollout marks the initial supervised deployment in the region and surfaces questions around system behavior on local roads with different signage and markings. It serves as a data collection testbed before broader European expansion. No unsupervised capability is included yet.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:51.960
Regulatory approval for supervised FSD in the Netherlands arrived before any other European country, yet the system still requires a driver ready to intervene at any moment. That gap between permission and true unsupervised operation is the real constraint on scaling Robotaxi economics.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:02:10.460
Until regulators accept zero human oversight on public roads, each new market adds only incremental data rather than a new revenue stream. The Netherlands rollout therefore functions as an early indicator of how quickly the model can adapt to European road conditions, without crossing into full autonomy.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:29.180
Tesla's approach relies on collecting edge cases from every supervised mile to train toward unsupervised capability. European roads introduce different signage, lane markings, and driver behavior than US training sets, so the Netherlands experience tests how rapidly the software adjusts to those variables.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:47.040
If interventions remain low, the data collected could accelerate approval in neighboring countries. That same regulatory caution appears in California, where Tesla just lost access to state EV purchase incentives. California excluded Tesla from its latest EV incentive program.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:55.000
Buyers in the state lose direct purchase subsidies that remain available to competitors. No official reason was detailed in the filing.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:01.700
The change narrows Tesla's price advantage in its largest US market and could slow retail momentum there.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:14.740
Tesla has not commented on whether it will adjust pricing or financing offers to offset the change. While policy supports shifts at home, Tesla's energy business continues to land large utility scale projects.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:21.580
A Megapack installation in Poway supplies backup power equivalent to 385,000 homes.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:30.140
The project adds to Tesla energy's growing utility scale footprint in California. No capacity figure in megawatt hours was released.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:39.880
The deployment continues the pattern of large battery systems providing grid support during peak demand or outages. Energy storage is scaling in the real world.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:52.680
Robotics still needs to clear a higher bar according to one major bank. Morgan Stanley analysts stated Tesla must demonstrate working optimist units at scale before valuation models can incorporate robotics revenue.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:59.600
The note highlights the gap between prototype videos and factory output. No price target change was announced.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:06.560
The assessment focuses on the difference between early demonstrations and repeatable production volumes that could affect future earnings.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:16.400
While optimist waits for proof, cybercab test units are already appearing in multiple cities. A group of cybercabs was photographed parked together in Nashville.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:26.480
An owner filmed a cybercab traveling toward downtown Chicago from the suburbs. A refreshed cybercab prototype appeared with Starlink hardware integrated for connectivity.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:35.820
The addition suggests Tesla is testing satellite fallback for areas without cellular coverage. No delivery timeline was attached to the images.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:47.240
The vehicles remain in testing configurations as production and regulatory paths continue to develop. Retail expansion pairs with small but practical product updates for existing owners.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:05:01.620
Tesla will open its first Shikoku showroom on August 28 inside a major Ehime shopping mall. The location expands the brand's physical presence across Japan's four main islands. No sales volume targets were disclosed.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:09.680
The new site follows the pattern of placing showrooms in high traffic retail centers to reach customers who may not visit dedicated service centers.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:17.740
newer model Y vehicles in the US and Puerto Rico now support vehicle to load power export via an $80 adapter.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:27.580
The same update adds a factory under seat storage tray option priced at $40. The tray fits beneath the front seats and provides concealed cargo space.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:37.860
Availability is limited to recent builds. Some owners of recent model Y builds discovered their vehicles cannot use the new V2L adapter despite the software update.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:46.340
The incompatibility has prompted questions about which VIN range is qualified. Tesla has not issued a broader compatibility list.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:52.120
The changes give model Y owners access to features previously limited to other electric vehicles.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:06:01.980
Before we go, reports point to a possible next-gen roadster unveiling later this month with SpaceX thrusters. And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news.

